    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/b9q67OPtdsA",
      "title": "Indiana Jones 6 (2026) – First Trailer | Harrison Ford & Chris Pratt – Concept",
      "year": 2025,
      "duration": 2,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/b9q67OPtdsA/maxresdefault.webp",
      "desc": "#indianajones #harrisonford #chrispratt  Indiana Jones 6 (2026) – First Trailer | Harrison Ford & Chris Pratt – Concept  Legends don't just fade away. They get dragged back in when it matters most. This fan-made trailer imagines Indiana Jones 6 for 2026, with the legendary archaeologist much older now, trying to stay out of trouble. But when rumors start circulating about an ancient Egyptian relic called the Serpent's Crown—something powerful enough to warp reality itself—Indy gets pulled back into the field whether he wants to or not. This time, he's working with Dr. Layla Al-Jahiz, a sharp, ambitious historian who doesn't quite share Indy's philosophy. While he thinks artifacts should be studied and protected, she sees them as opportunities—ways to change the world, maybe even control it. There's also Dr. Jax Heller, a younger academic who's basically grown up idolizing Indiana Jones. He's eager, maybe a little too eager, but what he lacks in field experience he makes up for in knowledge that could save their lives. The real threat is Kaelen Voss, the leader of a mysterious group called the Scions. Voss isn't just after power—he thinks the world is beyond saving and wants to use the Serpent's Crown to tear down reality and rebuild it his way. As the Scions get closer to their goal, the stakes become terrifyingly real. History isn't just at risk—existence itself is. The trailer shows what we love about Indiana Jones: chasing clues across the globe, exploring tombs buried under deserts and modern cities, narrow escapes through collapsing ruins, deadly traps, and those impossible moments where quick thinking is the only way out. There are also quieter scenes where Indy reflects on everything he's done and whether any of it still matters. This story is really about time—what's worth keeping, what we have to let go of, and what happens when the past won't stay in the past. Indy has to figure out if the world actually needs him anymore, or if this one last adventure is going to cost him everything. One artifact. One final chase. One man standing between reality and total collapse. Shot with IMAX cameras for that classic, grounded adventure feel, this concept brings back what made Indiana Jones great—mystery, danger, and heart over empty spectacle. Because some legends don't retire. They just face bigger problems.  Disclaimer: This is a fan-made concept trailer created for entertainment purposes only. It is not affiliated with Lucasfilm, Disney, or any official studio. All rights to Indiana Jones and related characters belong to their respective owners.  Made by: @fandomtopics  ▻ Follow us on: 📸 Instagram: fandomtopicsofficial 📘 Facebook: @Fandomtopics  Watch this fan-made trailer imagining Indiana Jones 6 (2026) — where history fights back, and legends make one final stand."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/Ba2eMxx0oHs",
      "title": "Indiana Jones Complete Blu-Ray Trailer - Steve Spielberg Movies HD",
      "year": 2012,
      "duration": 3,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Ba2eMxx0oHs/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "Subscribe to TRAILERS: http://bit.ly/sxaw6h Subscribe to COMING SOON: http://bit.ly/H2vZUn Like us on FACEBOOK: http://goo.gl/dHs73 Follow us on TWITTER: http://bit.ly/1ghOWmt Indiana Jones Complete Blu-Ray Trailer - Steve Spielberg Movies HD  In June of 1981 director Steven Spielberg and executive producer George Lucas introduced the world to Indiana Jones when the unforgettable Raiders of the Lost Ark debuted in theaters. Exploding to instant acclaim, the film has now been carefully restored, alongside remastered versions of the archaeologist's other thrilling adventures—Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom, Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade and Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull. Prepare for excitement, adventure and snakes—why did it have to be snakes?—all with pristine picture and sound when INDIANA JONES: The Complete Adventures debuts on Blu-ray September 18,  from Lucasfilm Ltd. and Paramount Home Media Distribution.  Supervised by director Steven Spielberg and renowned sound designer Ben Burtt, Raiders of the Lost Ark has been meticulously restored with careful attention to preserving the original look, sound and feel of the iconic film. The original negative was first scanned at 4K and then examined frame-by-frame so that any damage could be repaired.  The sound design was similarly preserved using Burtt's original master mix, which had been archived and unused since 1981. New stereo surrounds were created using the original music tracks and original effects recorded in stereo but used previously only in mono. In addition, the sub bass was redone entirely up to modern specifications and care was taken to improve dialogue and correct small technical flaws to create the most complete and highest quality version of the sound possible while retaining the director's vision. The result is an impeccable digital restoration that celebrates the film and its place in cinematic history.  The installments in the franchise have won a combined seven Academy Awards®. Relive every heart-pounding thrill like never before as all four films arrive together, for the first time presented in 1080p high definition with English 5.1 DTS-HD Master Audio accompanied by a collection of documentaries, interviews, featurettes and new bonus features."
    },
