      "desc": "BREAKING: Cambodia and Thailand have agreed to an \"immediate and unconditional ceasefire\" with effect from midnight tonight, the leaders of Cambodia, Thailand and Malaysia have said in a joint statement.  *****  Malaysia’s Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim is mediating peace talks between Thai and Cambodian leaders on Monday (Jul 28), aimed at securing a ceasefire in their fierce border conflict. He is holding a press conference on the talks.  Both the United States and China ambassadors to Malaysia were also present at the peace talks in Malaysia's administrative capital of Putrajaya, a Malaysian official said.  Live updates: https://cna.asia/453olvm  Thailand and Cambodia had accused each other of starting the conflict last week and then escalating the clashes with heavy artillery bombardment at multiple locations along their 817-km land border, the deadliest conflict in more than a decade between the Southeast Asian neighbours.  Tensions between Thailand and Cambodia intensified since the killing in late May of a Cambodian soldier during a brief skirmish.  Subscribe to our channel here: https://cna.asia/youtubesub   Visit our website: https://cna.asia Download our app: https://cna.asia/app  Get our editors' picks of stories via chat apps: Telegram: https://cna.asia/telegram WhatsApp: https://cna.asia/whatsapp  Follow us on these platforms: https://www.facebook.com/channelnewsasia https://www.instagram.com/channelnewsasia  https://www.tiktok.com/@channelnewsasia"
