      "year": 2022,
      "duration": 12,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/GqQN_-eOLxk/maxresdefault.webp",
      "desc": "This covers the gamut of many astute observations and Easter Eggs found throughout the Indiana Jones series. Starting in 1981 and all the way to the latest film in the series, Dial of Destiny. Each film in the series has something that references other franchises but often, it references its sister series, Star Wars.     George Lucas's Indiana Jones got inspiration was from matinée serials from the 1930s. It takes inspiration from Hiram Bingham (National Geographic's first archaeological grantee), Roy Chapman Andrews, and Sir Leonard Woolley. Lucas used them as a template to use as the titular hero in the action film.   It has been 15 years since the release of the last Indiana Jones film in 2008. Now, in 2023, the final film featuring Harrison Ford was directed not by Steven Spielberg but by a much younger director named James Mangold, who also was the man behind \"Logan\", \"3:10 To Yuma\" and \"I Walk The Line.\" The final film, “Indiana Jones and The Dial of Destiny” will be released on June 30th.      Subscribe: http://bit.ly/Subscribe-to-Screenrant   Chapters:  0:00 - Intro  0:12 - R2D2 And C3PO Made A Cameo In Raiders Of The Lost Ark.  0:51 - The Beards Aka Spielberg And Lucas Make A Cameo 1:25 - The “Carboneto” Barrels 2:12 - Elaborate Fight sequence Cancelled Because of #2 2:53 - The Airplane’s Registration Number 3:31 - Indy Is Named After Lucas’s Dog (So Was Chewie).  4:21 - Pat Roach Is In All Three Original Three Movies.  5:18 - Dan Aykroyd Makes A Cameo In Temple Of Doom.  5:47 - Ford Pays Tribute To His Philosophy Professor 6:36  - Dial Of Destiny Airplane Resembles Hyperspace/Millennium Falcon.  7:06  - Sean Connery’s James Bond And Indy Wear Same Suit 7:46  - Deadly Lapel Flowers 8:28 - Henry Holds Newspaper Upside Down 9:07 - The Grail Holds Infinite Water 9:40 - Back Story for Indiana Jones   Check out Screen Rant’s official TikTok!  https://www.tiktok.com/@screenrant   Our Social Media: https://twitter.com/screenrant  https://www.facebook.com/ScreenRant   https://www.linkedin.com/company/screen-rant/   Our Website: http://screenrant.com/  Written by: Jeff J. Blix Narrated by: Joey Criscitello YouTube.com/OfficialJoeyC Edited by: Gullivar Du Katt  For copyright matters please contact us at: legal@valnetinc.com"
