    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/KiAWBkKe_z4",
      "title": "Does Dryden Vos have the Crystal Skull from Indiana Jones?",
      "year": 2025,
      "duration": 1,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KiAWBkKe_z4/sd2.jpg",
      "desc": "?sqp=-oaymwEoCIAFEOAD8quKqQMcGADwAQH4AbYIgAKAD4oCDAgAEAEYZSBbKEowDw==&rs=AOn4CLAYu-HehT5D8ddySgRVCzstxTlTAg Does Dryden Vos have the crystal skull from Indiana Jones in his office? No. I’ve seen a lot of people make that mistake, and for good reason. They look very close to one another. But Dryden’s skull is the masthead of Xim the Despot, which is a reference to one of the very earliest Star Wars books, Han Solo and the Lost Legacy. That book is about Han Solo’s search for the lost treasure of an ancient warlord named Xim. So the skull in Dryden’s office is just a fun easter egg. But if you’re disappointed that it wasn't the skull from Indiana Jones, don’t worry! Because you can still find it in Star Wars in The Clone Wars episode Wookiee Hunt. #starwars   Subscribe for more Star Wars videos every day! Join this channel to get access to perks: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCIKlsX1qfGqKPt4KAW-JOZg/join Support the channel: https://www.patreon.com/starwarsexplain Tiktok: https://www.tiktok.com/@starwarsexplain Instagram: http://instagram.com/starwarsexplained Twitter: https://twitter.com/StarWarsExplain Second channel: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5KUexDNjIDcGPz4nAY9mBw Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/groups/starwarsexplained Discord: https://discord.gg/ZPwEnDT Thumbnails by: https://twitter.com/bryaneward  Mailing Address Star Wars Explained 1227 Rockbridge Rd SW Ste 208 PMB 264 Stone Mountain, GA 30087  This channel is not affiliated in any way with Lucasfilm Ltd. LLC, The Walt Disney Company, or any of their affiliates or subsidiaries."
