    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/KUOyR2KG7r0",
      "title": "INDIANA JONES - FATE OF ATLANTIS - AI Movie Trailer!",
      "year": 2024,
      "duration": 3,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KUOyR2KG7r0/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "Another passion project I've been itching to scratch for years, now finally capable with AI! A trailer for the best Indiana Jones movie that never was, Fate of Atlantis.   Whatever your feelings on AI filmmaking, this is one of the ways I feel it can be super useful.. in crafting concepts that just wouldn't exist otherwise. It's not stepping on anyone's toes, not stealing anyone's work or taking away jobs, just bringing to life something that would never exist in the \"real world\" otherwise.  If you're an old school gamer like me and ever played one of the best point and clicks of all time, and undoubtedly one of the best Indy games to date, you'll appreciate how awesome Fate of Atlantis actually was. Using AI tools and a lot of graphical tweaking, I was able to piece together a trailer for how a film adaption of it might actually look.  This was a HELL OF A LOT of fun to work on, and hopefully there's some fellow Indy fans out there who appreciate it too! I drew on inspirations obviously from the game itself, as well as other Indy movies, and even the comic book adaption they released in the early 90's. Needless to say, I did my homework :D  Features two INCREDIBLE versions of the famous theme, from two truly amazing musicians, opening with a BEAUTIFUL orchestral cover by the amazingly talented Kokkinis Sound, found here.. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d57VxxP9G00&lc=Ugxh7fuo4JRoUDuYn414AaABAg.AAx7WTgRNO6AAykwwODbuj&ab_channel=KokkinisSound  ...and ramps up to epic proportions with a FANTASTIC energy pumping rendition by the awesome Krutikov Music, found here.. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ALQaMrqp7Vo&lc=Ugx4gd781Y2lgkdoYwR4AaABAg.AAx852ELnLWAAz0sLNEKZH&ab_channel=KrutikovMusic  Both were used with their extremely kind permission, and I sincerely thank them wholeheartedly. Their remarkable talent made the trailer better than it had any right to be! Do check out the other sublime compositions on their pages!   TOOLS USED – Minimax for the renders, Photoshop for the visuals, 11Labs for the voices, FreeSound for the SFX, and the amazing aforementioned composers for the music.  Lemme know what you think, and if you'd like to see more projects like this in future!   Warmest, Andi  Indiana Jones, Fate of Atlantis, AI, AI Filmmaking, Adventure game, Point and Click, Amiga, PC, Dos, Scumm, Movie Trailer, Lucasarts Games, Lucasfilm  #IndianaJones, #Atlantis, #AI,"
    },
