      "url": "https://youtu.be/lSYr2cU9dyE",
      "title": "The Secret Genius Behind Indiana Jones's Costumes",
      "year": 2025,
      "duration": 17,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lSYr2cU9dyE/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "In this all-new episode of Cinema Relics Investigates, host Dan Lanigan and the team go deep into one of the most legendary outfits in film history — the costume of Indiana Jones.  This isn’t just a hero’s wardrobe — it’s a hybrid costume that connects directly to three of the five films in the franchise and remained in use nearly as long as Harrison Ford’s own run as Indy. From Raiders of the Lost Ark to Dial of Destiny, this remarkable costume holds clues, mysteries, and a few surprises that even Indy himself would appreciate.  Dan and the crew take you on a sensory-driven journey that explores the materials, history, and smell of the costume (yes, smell), providing an unprecedented look at Indy’s pants, shirt, and leather jacket. Along the way, they make new discoveries that rewrite what we thought we knew about one of cinema’s most iconic looks.  Join us for this ongoing adventure as we reveal the truth behind the props we love! If you’re a movie buff, collector, or just love behind-the-scenes Hollywood history, you won’t want to miss this.   ✨ Props. Legends. Leather. Come get a whiff of adventure  Chapters:  00:00 – Introduction 01:05 – History: How the Indiana Jones Costume Evolved 02:00 – The Smell Test: What Adventure Really Smells Like 02:56 – Provenance: Tracking the Costume’s Origins 03:46 – Materials Review: Breaking Down Indy’s Gear 06:28 – Screen Matching the Jacket 08:17 – Screen Matching the Shirt 12:43 – Use in Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny 13:34 – The Jacket Timeline: A Costume Across Three Films 15:42 – Outro: Reflections on a Relic  FOLLOW US: Instagram: /cinemarelics Facebook: /cinemarelics  X / Twitter:  TikTok: /@cinemarelicsarchives   #CinemaRelicsInvestigates #IndianaJones #DanLanigan #MovieProps #BehindTheScenes #ScreenUsed #AdventureSmellsLikeThis #RaidersOfTheLostArk #TempleOfDoom #LastCrusade #DialOfDestiny"
