      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/oRsV_pBT0QM/maxresdefault.webp",
      "desc": "While watching the live Ring camera from my paddle rental business in Hale'iwa along with live TV news coverage, I realized that the Ring camera showed the Tsunami surges better than any of the footage shown on the live news channels, so I posted a timelapse on YouTube.  The ring camera on the Blue Planet Adventure Company deck captured the July 29,  Tsunami with water first rushing out of Anahulu River in Haleiwa, on the North Shore of Oahu, Hawaii, showing a first surge, then a second bigger surge.  After all the warnings we were worried that this could have been much worse and watching live as the water kept rising was stressful, it’s no joke watching your livelihood almost get washed away.  We got lucky this time with no major damage, if the water came up another foot it would have been a whole different story. Thank you for watching, stay safe.  If you are interested in paddling with us, please visit: http://www.blueplanetadventure.com   We hope you liked the video, please give it a thumbs up and subscribe to the blueplanetsurf YouTube channel, we post a new video every Saturday morning, Aloha!  Please come visit one of our shops on Oahu: Hale'iwa shop and rental location: Blue Planet Hale'iwa 62-620F Kamehameha Highway Haleiwa, Hawaii 96712 Tel (808) 888 0786 Open daily, 9 am to 5 pm http://www.blueplanetadventure.com  Honolulu store- - Hawaii's SUP and Foil HQ: Blue Planet Surf  1221 Kona St Honolulu, Hi 96814 Tel (808) 596 7755  open 10 am to 5 pm Hawaii Time, closed Wednesdays and Sundays http://www.blueplanetsurf.com  Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/bpsurf/ Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/blueplanetsurf  Find Paradise Aloha!  Search terms:  Hawaii Tsunami, tsunami video footage, tsunami timelapse, water surge, tsunami surge, live footage, blue planet adventure, rainbow bridge, SUP rental, Tsunami Hawai’i, hawaii tsunami, tsunami hawaii, tsunami , hawaii live cam, hawaii tsunami video footage youtube, live tsun