      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/Pk28YR3uVT4/maxresdefault.webp",
      "desc": "This is a re-edit of three episodes of the Young Indiana Jones TV series into a feature film telling the story of Indy's hunt for the Jackal's Head and his decision to fight in WW1. The story here acts as a prequel to the main Indiana Jones films, and my next re-edit will be The Treasure of The Peacock's Eye: starting in WW1 and following Indy's search for the diamond at the start of Temple of Doom, the first Indy movie chronologically, in 1935.  The three episodes that make up this film are:  \"My First Adventure\" - 1908 - Indy meets Lawrence of Arabia on an excavation in Egypt where a man is murdered and a valuable artefact is stolen. This segment has been completely reworked with new title sequence, intro, music, and effects shots to act as a kind of prologue, similar to the 1912 segment in The Last Crusade, and lasts for about 15 minutes.  \"The Curse of the Jackal\" - 1916 - Indy's travels to Mexico and joining the revolution with Pancho Villa, eventually lead him back to the stolen Jackal head he last saw as a boy. While fighting in the revolution, Indy and his new friend Remy watch footage of WW1 and decide they want to join up and fight.  \"Love's Sweet Song\" - 1916 - Indy and Remy return to England where they sign up to join the army. Before leaving for the front Indy falls in love.  New music, foley, sound effects, editing, title text and more has been painstakingly added and mixed to make this re-edit look and feel as much like a traditional Indiana Jones film as possible.  A full list of all changes will be made available in due course. ➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖➖"
