      "desc": "🤠 “Fortune and glory, kid. Fortune and glory.”  One of the most iconic and instantly recognisable movie props ever made, this is Harrison Ford’s screen-used eight-foot bullwhip, belt, and whip holster from Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade (1989). More than just a tool, Indy’s whip is woven into the DNA of the character and a symbol of his quick thinking, daring escapes, and pure cinematic adventure that has thrilled audiences for decades.  This eight-foot model, hand-braided by master whip maker David Morgan, was custom-made for The Last Crusade. Paired with the original whip belt and holster, this set was used during filming, including the iconic motorcycle chase sequence shot in Northern California. It still bears its original production prop tag and comes with a call sheet from that shoot.  One of the finest Indiana Jones bullwhips ever offered at public auction – and the only known eight-foot example accompanied by its original belt and holster – this is a museum-worthy piece of adventure film history. Make sure you check it out in our #PropstoreLiveAuction now 👉 https://bit.ly/emla_summer_  #IndianaJones #HarrisonFord #LastCrusade #MovieProps #FilmHistory #FilmProps #Propstore #IndyFans #AdventureMovies #MovieCollector"
