      "year": 2024,
      "duration": 0,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/QhxCVRJrVHs/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "Welcome to the LIVE animal camera in my backyard, which constantly streams my feeding station.    My name is Scott, and I live in a suburban neighborhood in northeast Ohio, near Cuyahoga Valley National Park. This animal cam provides entertainment and a chance to learn about the wildlife of the eastern USA.  DONATIONS ACCEPTED: Never required, but always appreciated. All funds go towards purchasing bird food. Thank you in advance!  https://www.paypal.com/paypalme/birdwatchinghq  You can expect to see Eastern Gray Squirrels, Eastern Chipmunks, and many different species of birds (Northern Cardinal, Blue Jay, American Crow, Mourning Dove, sparrows, and sometimes even Mallard ducks).  MORE ABOUT MY FEEDING STATION: I live in a suburban neighborhood in northeast Ohio, close to the Cuyahoga Valley National Park. I have been feeding the wildlife in my backyard for a few years and am still amazed at the incredible variety of species that visit. My goal is to keep transforming our one-acre yard into a place that attracts animals and birds by planting native plants and providing shelter (such as nest boxes and brush piles)  Please remember that this camera is situated only about 100 feet from the back door of my house. It's common to see my dog running around, my kids playing and saying something to the cameras, or me filling the feeders. I'm sorry if we accidentally scare away something you were watching. :)  WATCH MY BIRD FEEDER CAM, which is located above this one:  https://geni.us/livebirds    \"Have a great day filled with smiles and kind people\" - R.I.P. Bree  #animalcam #live #animals #wildlife #nowplaying"
