    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/Rztl7GyHShA",
      "title": "#CouldBeSunnyOrGizmo❓ Supplanted By Shadow & Jackie⚔ Talons Up❗️🛡@FOBBVCAM 2025-11-30",
      "year": 2025,
      "duration": 5,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Rztl7GyHShA/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "On November 30 we observed a quick but dramatic encounter when a Juvenile Bald Eagle (Juvenile = first year bird, hatched in ) followed Shadow to the nest. That time Shadow had a stick instead of fish in his talons and quickly supplanted the visitor off the nest to the lower branch. Jackie followed up, supplanting the Juvie off the nest tree completely.   Bald Eagle talons are their main weapon of choice. Notice how Jackie was aiming at the Juvie with her talons and the youngster was wise to avoid the danger completely by retreating away from the tree.  These decisive and assertive actions mean that Jackie and Shadow consider the tree their defensible territory. This should put everyone's minds at ease regarding potential alternative nest or picking a different nesting tree. Jackie and Shadow have spoken!  Field marks for Juvenile Bald Eagle: - smooth trailing edge of the wing, no signs of molt (the most decisive field mark) - dark crown - dark belly with no signs of molt  In other news, the Ojai Raptor Center recently released a Juvenile Bald Eagle in the Big Bear area on 11/30/. The released bird was banded but the visitor does not appear to have bands, so it's probably a different individual.  As always, there is no way to know for sure whether it was Sunny or Gizmo. There are simply too many active nesting territories in SoCal nowadays that produce too many chicks per year. 🙃 It's great to see them all striving, trying to steal feeesh and sometimes even getting the boot from the active nesting territories. It's all part of being an eagle!  🪶Raptor Plumage Vocab: Juvenile = 1st year, Immature = either Juvenile or Sub-Adult, Sub-Adult = between Juvenile & Adult, Adult = Definitive plumage (4-5 years) https://bit.ly/3tcOWHe  🪶Bald Eagle Molting Sequence & Aging https://bit.ly/3VdV6Rc  ℹResident Bald Eagle male: Shadow (unbanded) since May 2018. Estimated hatch year: 2014 ℹResident Bald Eagle female: Jackie (unbanded) since September 2016. Estimated hatch year: 2012  Original live video courtesy of  @FOBBVCAM   https://www.friendsofbigbearvalley.org/ The opinions presented here do not necessarily reflect the opinions of FOBBV.  FOBBV Recap report:  https://www.friendsofbigbearvalley.org/recap/"
