    {
      "url": "https://youtu.be/uDtaYHaDG9w",
      "title": "I left Indian to live with 30 strangers in Thailand!!",
      "year": 2025,
      "duration": 2,
      "poster": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uDtaYHaDG9w/maxresdefault.jpg",
      "desc": "Life at an engineering college but with adult money haha 😅  So, this was my first time staying at a co-living, co-working space so I already had a lot of apprehensions. (It’s a concept where you have a private room with access to shared spaces like co working area, kitchen, living room etc).  On top of that, as I entered all I could see were men. I was later told that somehow we have 25 men and just 5 women at the co-living for now.  As someone who was constantly surrounded by beautiful female friendships this year, it was super new for me. But omg in no time, we were doing dinners, cooking, games, movie nights even weekend trips together. It was super cute to see them being excited about getting their pictures clicked on the trip.  Or to hear about their ambitions, love stories, life back home and everything in between. I don’t know what it was about each of them, but it was so effortless to confide in them and open up. Also, I was almost the only one cooking in the kitchen but never felt like that thanks to the company!  In just a few days, they gave me the space to express without judgements and JUST BE. They don’t even realise how healing just that presence was. Grateful for the friendships travel can make you experience. Always rooting for each one of them! Whether in the video or now, you know who you are ❤️❤️  Coliving space- @thesocialclub.asia  Ps- Happy men’s day (belated). Here’s to male friendships that make travel and life a little better. #chiangmai #thailand #malefriendship #mensday"
    },
